ILC pads code sections to the node alignment with a single byte: NOP on
x86/x64, zero elsewhere. On riscv64 that leaves 0x00000000 words between
methods (about two per method), which is not an instruction. SP1 eagerly
transpiles every word of every PF_X segment and panics on the first one it
cannot decode ("Cannot decode instruction: 0x0"), so no bflat guest loads
there; ZisK/OpenVM only tolerate the zeros because they are never executed.
Pad riscv64 code with a real NOP (addi x0, x0, 0 = 0x00000013) instead:
SectionData takes a padding pattern and keeps it in phase with the section
offset.

